## Why Each Element Was Added

### Load Balancer (HAProxy)
Added to distribute incoming traffic across multiple servers. Without it, all traffic hits a single server — creating a bottleneck and SPOF. HAProxy sits in front of both servers and routes requests intelligently, improving availability and performance.

### 2 Servers (instead of 1)
Added to eliminate the single point of failure from Task 0. If Server 1 fails, Server 2 continues to handle requests. Two servers also double the compute capacity for handling concurrent requests.

### Nginx (Web Server) on each server
Each server needs its own Nginx instance to handle HTTP requests, serve static files, and proxy dynamic requests to the local application server.

### Application Server on each server
Each server runs its own application server to process business logic independently. This enables parallel request processing and horizontal scalability.

### Application Files (Codebase) on each server
Both servers must have the same codebase deployed so they can serve identical responses regardless of which server handles the request.

### MySQL Primary-Replica Cluster
A single database would be a SPOF. The Primary-Replica setup ensures the data layer has redundancy: the Replica can be promoted if the Primary fails. It also allows read traffic to be distributed to the Replica, reducing load on the Primary.

