## Active-Active vs Active-Passive

### Active-Active (this infrastructure)
Both servers are **simultaneously active** and handling real user traffic. The load balancer distributes requests across all active nodes.
- **Pros:** Maximum resource utilization; full horizontal scaling; no idle capacity
- **Cons:** Requires session synchronization; both servers must be identical in config and code

### Active-Passive
One server is **active** (handling traffic), the other is **passive** (standby). The passive server only receives traffic if the active server fails.
- **Pros:** Simpler to manage; no synchronization needed during normal operation
- **Cons:** 50% of capacity sits idle; failover takes time (brief downtime during switch)

**This infrastructure uses Active-Active** — both servers handle live traffic simultaneously.

